  "finding": "In click_only spans the high-frequency novelty peak picker (threshold max(3*median, 4% max)) returns 2-10x more peaks than clicks (151 for 50 clicks; 296 for 30) because fan-noise peaks pass the adaptive threshold when no attack sets the maximum. The median-IOI grid seed is then taken from spurious intervals (0.23 s, 0.21 s and 0.185 s against P = 0.4, 0.4 and 0.6757 s), or the second span's coverage collapses (5503: 2/7 retained), giving click_grid_not_fitted. Click SNR was 12.6-15.3 dB, so these were not masking cases. Dev seeds 11-13 did not show the failure.",
  "consequence": "Where a grid fitted, the estimator, bias recovery and direction rule stayed within bounds. The failure is in the robustness of click-grid seeding."
